<title>USA: USDA to change export promotion program terms.</title>
<headline>USDA to change export promotion program terms.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it drafted approval criteria and weighting factors for trade groups competing for funds from the Foreign Market Development Cooperator Program.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, the agency's Foreign Agricultural Service asked for public comments on the proposal by June 16.</p>
<p>The program, which has existed since 1978, is designed to expand foreign markets for U.S. commodities and products. It provides funds for promotional activities for non-profit producer groups.</p>
<p>USDA's proposed criteria include the applicant group's past export performance and the dollar value of projected world imports of a particular commodity.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8467))</p>
